{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mass.UICPerBlockLogSymmetryCurvature","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mass.UICPerBlockLogSymmetryCurvature","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Log.Basic","lean:module:QOU.Mass.UICPerBlockLogPairTerm"],"declarations":2,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.UICPerBlockLogSymmetryCurvature.allPairs_additive_secondDiff_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.UICPerBlockLogSymmetryCurvature.allPairs_additive_secondDiff_pos","kind":"theorem","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/UICPerBlockLogSymmetryCurvature.lean#L79-L88","doc":"The same statement read through `census_secondDiff`: the all-pairs additive binding is\n**strictly convex** in `Z`, so the symmetric nucleus is a strict minimum — an anti-valley,\nnot a valley of stability. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.UICPerBlockLogSymmetryCurvature.symmetryCurvature_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.UICPerBlockLogSymmetryCurvature.symmetryCurvature_pos","kind":"theorem","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/UICPerBlockLogSymmetryCurvature.lean#L58-L77","doc":"**The `pn` letter's position forces an anti-valley.** With bond factors `b > 0` and the\nadditive letters `L = −log b`, if the `pn` factor is at least the midpoint of the `pp` and\n`nn` factors — which convention D guarantees via `ChainTraceFactor.deltaPN_nonneg` — and the\n`pp` and `nn` factors differ, then `L_pp + L_nn − 2·L_pn > 0`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}